			<div class="content" id="post-content-4594595">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> War</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The US Government tries to handle a large scale anomaly on its own, the Foundation has to clean up the mess.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> In the 1920s, a small Neo-Sarkic began to grow in power and influence in southern Nevada. The US government offers to keep outsiders away, in exchange the Sarkics will not try to secure more influence in Nevada and will offer their skills to aid American medical advances. This goes on until a few of the cult's younger members go off to help the US in WW2, none return. Then in 1950, much more aggressive members of the Cult decide to seek revenge against the US. They kidnap some locals and turn them into Sarkic monsters to wreak havoc, the UIU, as well as US soldiers in the area, try to put down the revolt but are only good at halting its advance rather than outright crushing it. They attempt to send negotiators to find a peaceful solution but, upon arrving, the negotiators are slaughtered. Eventually, in 1951, the military nukes the region they controlled. The US and Foundation launch a mass amentising campaign and the area is declared a nuclear test site. Surviving cultists request a return to the status quo, but the US Government refuses and cuts them off.</p>
<p>The Foundation now contains any surviving Sarkic creatures.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Seeing how the US tries to handle a major anomaly, and its aftermath, through the lens of the Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The US government did not call upon the Foundation or the GOC until post nuking because they wanted to prove to the world of the anomalous that they could be independent of these groups and handle it themselves.</p>
<p>The actual item itself are several creatures related to this event, the plot is told through interviews, journals and briefings.</p>
<p>I am considering making this a tale but I am unsure at this time.</p>

