															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="5869409"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1586824545 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Apr 2020 00:35</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4594659">
									

<p>Hm. I&#8230; don't know. It's interesting to actually see the USGOV declaring &quot;war&quot; on the Proto-Sarkicists, and the Foundation's view on that, but I'm not sure if the Foundation basically possessing a third party role during most of the conflict (that is, until before the nukes) would merit itself as an article? This actually sounds a lot more like a non-SCP article work, like a tale, or an incident report. There, you could explore into the hatred that the Sarkicists have against the USGOV and all.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I get the horror feeling you'd want to evoke out of, but broadening the scope of the issue really kinda sucks out any feelings of uneasiness/fear? I would figure horror does slightly better in tight, claustrophobic spaces instead of taking it nationwide, and ending it off with a nuke. If you're still willing to make this an SCP article, find a central theme/emotion you want to deliver, build your article around that theme, establish a sense of escalation up to the climax before ending it off. I'm not sure horror would fit(?) unless you just zoomed into one of the Sarkicist-controlled towns and how they live and all/an exploration by the MTF unit that goes horribly wrong/awry with the introduction of the creatures.</p>
<p>Idk, I would like to see a lot more Foundation intervention here other than helping the USGOV amnesticize possibly the entire US population.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>they wanted to prove to the world of the anomalous that they could be independent of these groups and handle it themselves.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds&#8230; weirdly childish? It's basically the USGOV wanting to prove to the Foundation that they're as good as them, only to horribly screw it up by nuking their own land.</p>
<p>A potential point of interest could be the hatred that the Sarkicists had towards the USGOV after WWII. You could focus on them being all friendly and all before WWII, before their relationship is severely strained as seen from various logs of meetings between the POTUS and the leader of the cults? It's your call on how you're going to go about doing this.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

