			<div class="content" id="post-content-4595375">
									

<p>Hm. My main gripe is that while you have a kinda interesting plot to carry out, I'm not sure what emotional impact you're trying to deliver here? Is it meant to be humorous? Or something else? Idk, basically ending it off with them nuking the Sarkicist-controlled areas feels rather&#8230; overexaggerated? I would rather envision the USGOV collaborating with the Foundation to perhaps send a diplomatic convoy to initiate peace talks between the ruler and the whoever's sent from the USGOV side. Though, that could just be me, I guess.</p>
<p>I was wondering if you could convey the extreme hatred that some of the Sarkicists expressed towards the USGOV about their failure to ensure the safety of the drafted Sarkicists through these diplomatic meetings instead? And then we could end it off on a rather grim/dark note, where the Sarkicists demand something in return, but the USGOV like, cuts them off and says that they never promised anything (or something along those lines) to them during the war, devastating the Sarkicists. This maybe could evoke some sad stuff, as well as the pain of the harsh reality that everyone had faced?</p>

