														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4622565">
									

<p>This is honestly amazing, in my opinion. Not only does this seem to play out like a novelization of a sci-fi movie, but I could just imagine the number of narrative opportunities you have with this. That said, I want you to be careful not to just make this about battles and not leave enough room for actual character development.</p>
<p>I haven't seen any SCPs where the actual US government is involved while the Foundation has to do things after them, that's actually a concept that I want to be written and executed well.</p>
<p>Though, I have to agree with MalyceGraves. It's gonna be hard to write the documents retroactively, but I will give you a touch of faith with this one. With stories like this, it's a little easy to fall into the temptation of writing an event in the story as a shortcut to proceed rather than having it connect with the events and the story overall.</p>
<p>I give you a <span style="color: green">greenlight.</span> Good luck, man. I'll look forward to this.</p>

							</div>

								
